      "explanation": "<b>Step 1 :</b> In step 1, NaNO<sub>2</sub> + HCl , 0-5°C used for diazotisation reaction. It will form diazonium salt. Further, it will react with KCN to form cyanobenzene.\n<br><br> <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kxhfe5p6/2cc4ac44-a9b9-4b5a-83b1-d05aa45072f3/7d8792b0-6316-11ec-b1e6-f1aee4474c98/file-1kxhfe5p7.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1kxhfe5p6/2cc4ac44-a9b9-4b5a-83b1-d05aa45072f3/7d8792b0-6316-11ec-b1e6-f1aee4474c98/file-1kxhfe5p7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 24th February Morning Shift Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 187 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1kxhfe5p6/2cc4ac44-a9b9-4b5a-83b1-d05aa45072f3/7d8792b0-6316-11ec-b1e6-f1aee4474c98/file-1kxhfe5p7.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1kxhfe5p6/2cc4ac44-a9b9-4b5a-83b1-d05aa45072f3/7d8792b0-6316-11ec-b1e6-f1aee4474c98/file-1kxhfe5p7.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1kxhfe5p6/2cc4ac44-a9b9-4b5a-83b1-d05aa45072f3/7d8792b0-6316-11ec-b1e6-f1aee4474c98/file-1kxhfe5p7.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1kxhfe5p6/2cc4ac44-a9b9-4b5a-83b1-d05aa45072f3/7d8792b0-6316-11ec-b1e6-f1aee4474c98/file-1kxhfe5p7.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1kxhfe5p6/2cc4ac44-a9b9-4b5a-83b1-d05aa45072f3/7d8792b0-6316-11ec-b1e6-f1aee4474c98/file-1kxhfe5p7.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1kxhfe5p6/2cc4ac44-a9b9-4b5a-83b1-d05aa45072f3/7d8792b0-6316-11ec-b1e6-f1aee4474c98/file-1kxhfe5p7.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n<br> <b>Step 2 :</b> In step 2, SnCl<sub>2</sub> and HCl is a Stephen’s reduction reagent. Cyanobenzene reduced